From: Nouveau debugging notes
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] nouveau: serialize VP3 teardown on separate channels

Mesa 26.0.8 experiment. For distinct BSP/VP/PPP channels, destroy each
engine object, then its push buffer, then its channel before moving to the
next engine. Preserve the original ordering for shared-channel hardware.
This changes teardown order only; it does not alter decode commands or kernel
recovery behavior. It remains unvalidated until a fresh-boot hardware A/B.

---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_vp3_video.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_vp3_video.c
@@ -283,39 +283,25 @@
    for (i = 0; i < NOUVEAU_VP3_VIDEO_QDEPTH; ++i)
       nouveau_bo_ref(NULL, &dec->bsp_bo[i]);
-
